cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this project or its VAN protocol findings, please cite it using the metadata below."

title: "Neru's 206 Dashboard"
abstract: |-
  Peugeot 206 (AEE2001 platform) instrument-cluster dashboard: two round displays
  driven by an ESP32-S3, reading rpm, coolant temperature, intake temperature via
  K-line OBD and vehicle speed from the VAN comfort bus.

  The repository mainly publishes an evidence-backed measured reference for the
  PSA / AEE2001 VAN comfort bus (frame layout, E-Manchester / 4B5B, CRC-15
  parameters, measured 8.25 us slot time, decoded IDs) plus the wiring notes,
  architecture decisions and per-run acceptance log behind it.

  Licensing is layered: code is MIT, documentation (*.md) is CC BY 4.0, and
  artwork / image and binary assets are declared separately with all rights
  reserved. The root LICENSE holds the plain MIT text only; the layered scope
  is stated in LICENSING.md, with licensing details in LICENSE-DOCS,
  LICENSE-ARTWORK and THIRD-PARTY.md. This mix is also why the entry below
  exists: the MIT license field of this software entry does not describe the
  documentation, which is cited separately as CC BY 4.0.

type: software
authors:
